<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ranuccio I Farnese, Duke of Parma</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1569">1569</a>–<a href="/years/1622">1622</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Ranuccio I Farnese</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ranuccio I Farnese was duke of Parma and Piacenza from 1592, the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alessandro-farnese-duke-of-parma">Alessandro Farnese</a>. He strengthened ducal power over the nobility, and in 1612 he executed several leading nobles, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barbara-sanseverino">Barbara Sanseverino</a>, for an alleged conspiracy and confiscated their estates. He built the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palazzo-della-pilotta">Palazzo della Pilotta</a> in Parma, with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teatro-farnese">Teatro Farnese</a> inside it.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ranuccio-i-farnese-duke-of-parma.jpg" alt="Ranuccio I Farnese, Duke of Parma" width="320" height="378" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Cesare Aretusi · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ranuccio_I_Farnese,_Duke_of_Parma_by_Cesare_Aretusi.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
